1
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:05,470
This concludes the data 
on Ayanokoji Kiyotaka

2
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:09,720
and the other 156 members 
of the second-year class.

3
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,290
Have you memorized all of it?

4
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:17,660
Your role is to have Ayanokoji-kun 
expelled within the month of April,

5
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:20,260
and return him to the White Room.

6
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:23,800
Be careful and clever in 
your pursuit of this goal.

7
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:27,060
If this becomes known, 
the name of that person...

8
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:31,130
of Sensei could be greatly damaged.

9
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:36,770
You seem displeased about this.

10
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:42,370
You don't think he deserves to 
be treated as our masterpiece?

11
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:45,740
Well, I've set the stage for you.

12
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,170
Let me see what you can do.

13
00:00:49,730 --> 00:00:54,960
With talent like yours, it should 
be easy to get him expelled.

14
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:59,230
I forgot to ask one thing...

15
00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:03,230
You're not hiding anything 
from me, are you?

16
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:13,000
A battle between students 
of the White Room—

17
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:15,620
Hunt or be hunted.

18
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:18,930
Though it's merely a 
game between children,

19
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:23,390
it could prove interesting.

20
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:30,630
#1 Assassin From the White Room

21
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:31,930
Hey, they turned the blackboard 
into a computer screen!

22
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:32,820
That's pretty cool!

23
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:34,380
Hey, Ayanokoji.

24
00:01:34,710 --> 00:01:35,490
Miyake.

25
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:40,630
You didn't come to group meetings 
much over spring break.

26
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:42,490
I was worried.

27
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:45,350
I'm sorry. I was a bit busy.

28
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:48,270
Obviously, you're under 
no obligation to come,

29
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:53,170
but Haruka, and especially Airi, 
seemed to miss you.

30
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:56,580
Sorry.

31
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:59,260
I'll try to show up 
more often from now on.

32
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:00,950
Hope so.

33
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:03,240
I like having you there, too.

34
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,710
What were you talking about?

35
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:06,650
Nothing.

36
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:09,400
S-Suzune?!

37
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:12,040
What's with the hair?!

38
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,900
Horikita-san, this is quite a new you!

39
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:18,150
Is it that unusual to see 
someone cut their hair?

40
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:22,630
N-Nah, I mean, I just didn't expect it.

41
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:25,410
It actually looks pretty 
great on you, too...

42
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:27,410
R-Right, Kushida?

43
00:02:27,410 --> 00:02:29,180
Yes, of course.

44
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:31,290
But what led you to do it?

45
00:02:31,290 --> 00:02:34,440
You may consider it a display 
of resolve, I suppose.

46
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:38,920
As we enter our second year, I intend 
to fight to raise Class D's ranking.

47
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:42,680
I am prepared to do whatever 
it takes to make that happen.

48
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:44,480
Oh, gotcha.

49
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:48,430
Maybe I'll grow my hair 
out to balance it out!

50
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:50,730
There's a lot of noise in here.

51
00:02:51,090 --> 00:02:52,550
Take your seats at once.

52
00:02:53,690 --> 00:02:55,900
I'd like to start by asking you to

53
00:02:55,900 --> 00:03:00,700
undergo a task crucial to your 
lives here moving forward.

54
00:03:00,970 --> 00:03:06,540
I want you to access the school's 
homepage and install a new app.

55
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:11,080
The app's official name 
is "Over All Ability."

56
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:15,710
OAA for short.

57
00:03:14,230 --> 00:03:15,710
An application to assess and rank all students in the following five categories:

58
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:15,710
Academic Achievement: Primarily reflects written test scores across the year.

59
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:15,710
Physical Ability: Reflects evaluations in gym class, club activities, and special tests.

60
00:03:14,390 --> 00:03:15,710
Situational Thinking: Reflects social proficiency, communication skills, and situational adaptability as
                           reflected in size of friend groups and position within them.

61
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:15,710
Prosocial Proficiency: Reflects contributions toward school community, including in-class attitude,
                           attendance, lack of problematic behavior, and student council affiliation.

62
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,710
General Evaluation: A reflection of the student's all-around ability calculated based on the four values
                   listed above (Prosocial Proficiency only counts half).

63
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:15,710
*General Evaluation =
(Academic Achievement + Physical Ability + Situational Thinking + Prosocial Proficiency*0.5) / 350 * 100 (rounded)

64
00:03:15,710 --> 00:03:17,460
OAA?

65
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:20,640
This app will be used by 
students in all years,

66
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:25,190
and it will provide you access 
to a variety of resources.

67
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:28,940
For instance, individual 
data on all students.

68
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,600
Have a look at your own data for starters.

69
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,270
T-Teacher!

70
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:37,360
It's giving me letter 
ranks like in a game!

71
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,850
That's right.

72
00:03:38,850 --> 00:03:43,010
These are individual assessments of 
your abilities made by the school

73
00:03:43,010 --> 00:03:45,140
based on your performance last year.

74
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:49,870
You can view the abilities of 
students in all years and classes.

75
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:53,370
I'm an E in academic achievement?

76
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:56,350
The ratings will be updated at 
the beginning of each month.

77
00:03:56,350 --> 00:03:59,210
Sudo, even if you're rated E right now,

78
00:03:59,210 --> 00:04:04,130
if you were to ace your next written 
test, you would be ranked an A+.

79
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:10,110
But a bad score will also linger 
as a blot on your record.

80
00:04:10,110 --> 00:04:13,140
And everyone in the school 
will be able to see it.

81
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:16,920
Remember that your first-year 
ratings simply represent the past.

82
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:20,150
They won't affect your 
evaluations moving forward.

83
00:04:20,150 --> 00:04:25,180
We hope that those with less than 
stellar marks will find new drive

84
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,660
to attempt to improve them.

85
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:30,860
<i>A convenient tool to check 
our accomplishments...</i>

86
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:33,290
<i>No, there's surely more to it than that.</i>

87
00:04:33,290 --> 00:04:35,580
This app represents equality.

88
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:37,610
We hope that being judged

89
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:42,860
on the same benchmarks will promote 
more interaction between class years.

90
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:44,100
However...

91
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:47,050
I believe there's more to it than that.

92
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:50,220
This is just my own hypothesis,

93
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:51,730
but I suspect that anyone

94
00:04:51,730 --> 00:04:55,190
whose General Evaluation does not meet a 
certain benchmark by the end of the year

95
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:58,520
will face some kind of penalty.

96
00:04:58,850 --> 00:05:02,530
Penalty? You mean... expulsion?

97
00:05:02,530 --> 00:05:04,820
A-Are you kidding me?!

98
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:07,980
I'm sure some of you may not 
be happy with your numbers,

99
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:10,830
but it's an evaluation of 
your current standings.

100
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:12,600
If you don't like it,

101
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:16,830
spend this year forcing the school 
to accept your true talents.

102
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:19,840
So we're fighting for ourselves.

103
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:22,700
<i>The integration of this 
app turns the concept</i>

104
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:25,500
<i>of fighting together 
as a class on its head.</i>

105
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:28,590
<i>Their fear and confusion 
is understandable.</i>

106
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:31,960
In addition, this system 
was adopted on the proposal

107
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:35,350
of the current student council 
president, Nagumo Miyabi.

108
00:05:35,350 --> 00:05:38,910
<i>Create a system where we're evaluated 
based on individual ability.</i>

109
00:05:38,910 --> 00:05:43,110
<i>Nagumo's putting his dream into reality.</i>

110
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:49,120
And your first special 
test of your second year

111
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:53,080
will include an unprecedented concept.

112
00:05:53,410 --> 00:05:58,530
You will partner up with the 
incoming class of first-years

113
00:05:58,530 --> 00:06:01,590
to take a written test.

114
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:04,710
Partner up with the first-years?

115
00:06:05,090 --> 00:06:09,620
Previously, the school hasn't encouraged 
interaction between class years.

116
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:14,470
We've deduced that this has hindered your 
development of communication skills.

117
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:18,950
B-But aren't we competing with 
other classes in our year?

118
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:21,820
It feels kinda weird, yeah.

119
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,330
Think about it.

120
00:06:23,330 --> 00:06:26,260
When you enter the real world, 
you won't always be interacting with

121
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:28,990
people from your graduating class.

122
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:33,660
And you may end up in competition with 
first-years and third-years at times.

123
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:38,390
You can work with anyone from 
any class in the first year.

124
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:40,540
The test will be at the end 
of the month in two weeks.

125
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:44,490
You'll have plenty of time 
to pick your partner.

126
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:47,860
<i>We haven't interacted 
with the first-years.</i>

127
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:51,010
<i>It will be difficult to build up a 
relationship of trust from nothing.</i>

128
00:06:51,010 --> 00:06:54,260
<i>Perhaps that's part of 
what the OAA app is for.</i>

129
00:06:54,260 --> 00:06:56,010
The test will cover five subjects,

130
00:06:56,010 --> 00:06:58,040
with a maximum score of 500 points.

131
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:00,540
And this is very important—

132
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:05,120
this time around, there will be 
incentives for success on both class

133
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,280
and individual levels.

134
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:10,280
I knew it. If you fail, you're expelled!

135
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:12,990
Partnerships must be 
formed by mutual consent,

136
00:07:12,990 --> 00:07:16,410
and once decided, 
cannot be undone for any reason.

137
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:20,090
I'm sure you've already realized that

138
00:07:20,090 --> 00:07:23,410
academically proficient students will 
be in high demand for this test.

139
00:07:24,070 --> 00:07:29,300
Ma'am, what will happen to students who 
can't find a partner before the test?

140
00:07:29,730 --> 00:07:33,900
The leftovers will be paired 
randomly on the day of the test.

141
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:35,480
That said,

142
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:38,830
a 5% penalty will be imposed on those who 
failed to find a partner on their own.

143
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:42,060
So you're in deep trouble 
if you don't find a partner!

144
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:48,490
Wh-Wh-What do we do, Hirata?!

145
00:07:48,490 --> 00:07:50,460
Who the heck in year one is 
gonna pair with someone

146
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:52,490
with an E in Academic Achievement?!

147
00:07:52,490 --> 00:07:54,700
I'm worried, too.

148
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,410
Calm down, everyone.

149
00:07:56,410 --> 00:07:58,370
Let's figure out our approach.

150
00:07:58,370 --> 00:08:01,410
Yes, there's no need to hurry.

151
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:04,720
The app sent us something along 
with the test conditions.

152
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:07,380
It's the predicted points for each
Academic Achievement rating.

153
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:10,750
The baseline for expulsion is 500 
points between you and your partner.

154
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:12,780
Someone with an E-level 
Academic Achievement

155
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:17,600
can work with someone of rank B or 
higher and easily clear the test.

156
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:19,900
Horikita-san is right.

157
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:22,100
If we work hard to prepare like always,

158
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,350
I'm sure we can all get 
through this again.

159
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:28,250
The most important thing is to be 
careful when choosing partners.

160
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:32,110
If you encounter any issues, 
talk to me or Hirata-kun.

161
00:08:34,110 --> 00:08:38,110
<i>Any student of any year found to be 
intentionally lowering their score</i>

162
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:40,810
<i>will be expelled immediately.</i>

163
00:08:41,450 --> 00:08:44,030
<i>That would normally be a 
significant deterrence.</i>

164
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:48,170
<i>But it won't apply to 
the White Room student.</i>

165
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:52,030
<i>If they manage to pair up with me,</i>

166
00:08:52,030 --> 00:08:55,460
<i>they won't hesitate to score a 
zero to take me down with them.</i>

167
00:08:56,010 --> 00:09:00,740
<i>In other words, if I choose the person 
from the White Room as my partner,</i>

168
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,350
<i>I'm done for.</i>

169
00:09:03,010 --> 00:09:08,980
<i>Acting Chairman Tsukishiro... 
I'm sure he came up with these rules.</i>

170
00:08:48,590 --> 00:08:59,100
Special Academic Test Outline.pdf
 Class Incentives
-Class score is determined from the average score of all class members and their partners. 
-Classes will be awarded the following class point totals based on their class score,
from highest to lowest: 50 points, 30 points, 10 points, 0 points.
Individual Incentives
-Individual score is the combined score of an individual and their partner.
 -The top five pairs will receive a reward of 100,000 private points each.
-The top 30% of pairs will be given 10,000 private points each.
 -If any pair scores a total of 500 or less, the second-year student will be expelled,
and the first-year student will not receive private points for three months
regardless of class point standings.
- Students found to be intentionally getting questions wrong to manipulate
or lower scores will be immediately expelled. Students found to be coercing
third parties into getting low scores will be likewise expelled.

172
00:09:15,990 --> 00:09:19,560
Do you remember our agreement 
over winter break,

173
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,120
that the two of us would compete?

174
00:09:21,570 --> 00:09:25,080
You think the upcoming special 
test is perfect for that?

175
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:28,850
Yes. If you win, 
I'll join the student council.

176
00:09:29,250 --> 00:09:32,980
If I win, you will henceforth use 
all of the talent you've been hiding

177
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,090
for the sake of our class.

178
00:09:35,490 --> 00:09:36,710
I have no objections.

179
00:09:37,090 --> 00:09:38,890
Good.

180
00:09:38,890 --> 00:09:41,770
Let's move to our next topic, then.

181
00:09:42,450 --> 00:09:43,820
I looked into first-year students

182
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:46,300
with an Academic Achievement 
rating of B or higher.

183
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:51,220
There are seventeen in Class A, 
thirteen each in Class B and C,

184
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:53,320
and eleven in Class D.

185
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:56,360
Fifty-four in total.

186
00:09:56,870 --> 00:10:00,530
We have only four students with 
an Academic Achievement of E.

187
00:10:00,530 --> 00:10:02,930
Twelve if we throw in those with D.

188
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:07,120
There are more than enough first-year 
students to fill the roles we need.

189
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:11,630
The question is how to get such 
excellent students to partner with

190
00:10:11,630 --> 00:10:13,590
students ranked D or E.

191
00:10:13,590 --> 00:10:18,840
Yes. I think Sudo-kun should 
be our first priority.

192
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:23,350
Hasn't his Academic Achievement 
been improving a lot?

193
00:10:23,350 --> 00:10:25,280
It has.

194
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:28,590
But if you'd never met either of them before,

195
00:10:28,590 --> 00:10:31,610
which would you rather pair with? 
Sudo-kun or Ike-kun?

196
00:10:31,610 --> 00:10:38,360
True. Sudo is physically imposing, 
sharp-tongued, and generally frightening.

197
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:43,360
Yes. Finding him a partner 
at all may prove difficult.

198
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:45,300
So I want to begin right away.

199
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,870
Will you help me?

200
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:53,380
Ichinose Honami
I've gotten permission to host a mixer between first-
and second-year students in the gym today starting at 4.
If you have time, we'd love to meet with you.

201
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:53,380
Ichinose-san is impressive, as always.

202
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:58,380
She's thinking not just of Class B, 
but the entire picture at once.

203
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:02,890
Class A and Class C will likely 
take their own measures.

204
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:06,740
I still don't know what Ryuen-kun 
and Sakayanagi-san will try.

205
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:12,020
But I think one potential avenue for 
negotiation would be private points.

206
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:15,190
You think we should attempt to bribe them?

207
00:11:15,190 --> 00:11:19,990
Yes, points are the most obvious 
asset we can offer to first-years.

208
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:22,260
Ideally, we would donate 
our personal funds

209
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:25,200
to secure a certain number of students...

210
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:30,100
But with our lower point incomes, 
it will be hard to play the money game.

211
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:32,460
I'll scout out the situation 
at the mixer first.

212
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:34,920
Understood. I'll come along.

213
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:37,830
Oh? You're cooperating, then?

214
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:43,180
I just want to see how you 
plan to approach this.

215
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:48,110
I see. I was hasty in using 
the word "cooperate."

216
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:55,690
Her first impulse is 
to build mutual trust.

217
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,690
That's rather typical of Ichinose-san.

218
00:11:58,690 --> 00:12:01,830
But shouldn't we get down there, then?

219
00:12:01,830 --> 00:12:04,450
What if Class B takes 
all the smart people?

220
00:12:04,810 --> 00:12:06,520
Do you think we could beat

221
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:09,950
Ichinose-san's team in a 
competition of social graces?

222
00:12:10,850 --> 00:12:12,660
It seems unlikely.

223
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:13,580
Let's go.

224
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:17,710
You sure about this, Suzune?

225
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:21,860
More than half of the students 
didn't attend the mixer.

226
00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:25,220
I want to speak to those who didn't.

227
00:12:27,070 --> 00:12:28,300
Didn't you notice?

228
00:12:28,630 --> 00:12:32,350
There's a bias among the 
students attending the mixer.

229
00:12:32,350 --> 00:12:33,850
Bias?

230
00:12:33,850 --> 00:12:38,360
There were no students from Class 1-D.

231
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,610
Izzat supposed to mean something?

232
00:12:40,610 --> 00:12:43,400
There are forty students in each class.

233
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,260
The fact that not a single one of them

234
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:48,870
attended suggests their 
class is acting as a unit.

235
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:52,150
In other words, Class 1-D 
already has a leader,

236
00:12:52,150 --> 00:12:55,120
and they decided to blow off the mixer.

237
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,110
Yes.

238
00:12:56,110 --> 00:12:58,890
If we can negotiate 
directly with that leader,

239
00:12:58,890 --> 00:13:01,400
we won't need to deal with individuals.

240
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:09,760
Hey. Ichinose's up to her old tricks, huh?

241
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:14,390
She seems to be focused first on saving 
her classmates and first-years.

242
00:13:14,390 --> 00:13:17,940
You think she realizes it's 
a drag to help out idiots?

243
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:20,150
It's basically throwing in the towel.

244
00:13:20,150 --> 00:13:25,750
Your Class A... Sakayanagi-san 
anticipated this, didn't she?

245
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:27,530
That's why you didn't participate.

246
00:13:27,530 --> 00:13:29,640
Yeah, I'd wager so.

247
00:13:30,030 --> 00:13:33,790
So how do you intend to bring 
the smart students to your side?

248
00:13:33,790 --> 00:13:36,750
That's up to Her Highness.

249
00:13:37,130 --> 00:13:39,790
I merely do as I'm told.

250
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,210
Let's hurry.

251
00:13:43,210 --> 00:13:47,340
The Class D students should still 
be in their classroom at this time.

252
00:13:52,510 --> 00:13:55,980
You're pretty late to the party, Suzune.

253
00:13:56,610 --> 00:13:57,860
Ryuen-kun.

254
00:13:57,860 --> 00:13:59,820
You also went to scout out the first-years

255
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:01,480
instead of attending the mixer?

256
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:06,360
The only ones going to the gym 
would be the class idiots.

257
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,490
I didn't need to look.

258
00:14:07,770 --> 00:14:09,990
You've already been to Class D?!

259
00:14:09,990 --> 00:14:13,990
Don't worry. 
I haven't won anyone over yet.

260
00:14:13,990 --> 00:14:17,380
Your attitude would just 
frighten the first-years.

261
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:22,000
I think a few light threats will 
get them on my side immediately.

262
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,550
You must be joking.

263
00:14:23,550 --> 00:14:25,760
You think that method would be allowed?

264
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:28,560
Can't imagine why it wouldn't be.

265
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:31,620
I didn't see a rule saying you're 
expelled for threatening someone

266
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:33,010
into being your partner.

267
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:35,770
It doesn't require a specific rule.

268
00:14:35,770 --> 00:14:38,350
If someone complains, 
you're the one who'll be affected.

269
00:14:38,350 --> 00:14:41,230
Complain and see what happens, then.

270
00:14:41,230 --> 00:14:44,900
Of course, I'm not so stupid 
as to leave tracks behind.

271
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:48,570
I'll give you a piece of info, though...

272
00:14:48,570 --> 00:14:53,370
Despite having just arrived, 
the first-years are extremely composed.

273
00:14:53,690 --> 00:14:55,370
What are you getting at?

274
00:14:55,770 --> 00:14:58,310
There's a very good chance 
that someone from the school

275
00:14:58,310 --> 00:15:04,130
has already explained to the 
newcomers how the school works.

276
00:15:05,630 --> 00:15:10,020
Well, good luck engaging with them.

277
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:15,930
The first-years might be more resistant 
to our efforts than expected.

278
00:15:15,930 --> 00:15:19,140
All the more reason to 
start negotiations now!

279
00:15:22,270 --> 00:15:24,270
What the hell is this?!

280
00:15:24,270 --> 00:15:28,400
Their class may be more difficult 
to deal with than anticipated.

281
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:39,450
<i>Notifications suggest that twenty-two 
pairs have formed as of this morning.</i>

282
00:15:40,070 --> 00:15:44,100
<i>If I draw the White Room spy, 
I'm expelled on the spot.</i>

283
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:48,290
<i>I've memorized the names and faces of 
all the first-years just in case, but...</i>

284
00:15:48,290 --> 00:15:49,510
Hey!

285
00:15:50,570 --> 00:15:52,510
Some first-years are heading our way!

286
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:13,060
I'm Nanase Tsubasa of Class 1-D.

287
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:15,030
And this is my classmate...

288
00:16:15,030 --> 00:16:16,780
Hosen.

289
00:16:17,190 --> 00:16:23,540
Freshmen don't usually come to an 
upperclassman's floor uninvited.

290
00:16:23,930 --> 00:16:25,750
I respect your boldness.

291
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:29,210
You respect it, huh?

292
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:30,260
You think you're better than us?

293
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:33,760
Get your head outta your 
ass, freshman punk.

294
00:16:35,370 --> 00:16:37,010
He's Academic Achievement E+.

295
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:39,810
You're as dumb as you look, then, huh?

296
00:16:39,810 --> 00:16:41,100
What was that?!

297
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:46,310
Figures, though. Class D are probably 
the only ones who'd come out to meet us.

298
00:16:46,310 --> 00:16:47,550
That suits us fine.

299
00:16:47,550 --> 00:16:49,560
What is that supposed to mean?

300
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:52,640
Your Class D's a group of failures.

301
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:56,490
You're not gonna make any decent 
pairings unless we come to you.

302
00:16:57,460 --> 00:17:01,380
So since you're all stupid and useless, 
we figured we'd lend a helping hand.

303
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:03,040
You get what I'm saying, right?

304
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:06,520
You want us to partner with you, then?

305
00:17:06,890 --> 00:17:08,790
That's quite a presumptuous way of asking.

306
00:17:08,790 --> 00:17:11,880
You're the ones who should be asking.

307
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:15,800
Go on, get on all fours and 
beg us to pair up with you.

308
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:17,340
You bastard—

309
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:19,950
You seem to be under a misapprehension.

310
00:17:19,950 --> 00:17:23,560
As a fellow Class D, 
we're on even footing with you.

311
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,140
Even footing, huh?

312
00:17:25,590 --> 00:17:27,440
You just don't get it.

313
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:31,020
We've got plenty of 
options if we want 'em.

314
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:33,150
We don't need to put up 
with bullshit, y'know?

315
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:38,530
<i>They seem to have noticed the special 
weapon unique to the first-years.</i>

316
00:17:38,530 --> 00:17:41,240
Just what method do you expect to use?

317
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:43,100
You get it, right?

318
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:46,750
We've got a way to force the scores down.

319
00:17:46,750 --> 00:17:49,430
What? Gimme a damn break!

320
00:17:49,430 --> 00:17:51,640
If you slack off on the test, 
your ass is expelled!

321
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:54,050
Yeah, if we do it by slacking off.

322
00:17:54,050 --> 00:17:57,640
But we can refuse to pair 
up until the day of the test

323
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,510
and force a penalty that way.

324
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:05,520
Since only second-years can be expelled, 
that hurts you way more than us.

325
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:10,270
Even if you aren't expelled, 
won't you face a loss of private points?

326
00:18:10,270 --> 00:18:14,050
Yeah, but that's a small price 
compared to the one you'll pay.

327
00:18:14,050 --> 00:18:14,610
Right?

328
00:18:14,610 --> 00:18:21,930
Yes. A three-month loss of private 
points is 240,000 points at most.

329
00:18:21,930 --> 00:18:24,750
I don't see it as a fatal issue.

330
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:28,280
You get the situation now?

331
00:18:29,310 --> 00:18:31,420
Get your head outta your ass.

332
00:18:31,890 --> 00:18:34,170
Keep your head, Sudo-kun.

333
00:18:34,170 --> 00:18:37,670
You know how things work 
at this school, don't you?

334
00:18:37,670 --> 00:18:39,680
Yeah, fine.

335
00:18:42,180 --> 00:18:44,180
Guess there's not much 
muscle on that big frame.

336
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:46,310
I barely even touched you.

337
00:18:46,310 --> 00:18:47,650
You son of a—

338
00:18:47,650 --> 00:18:48,940
What are you doing?!

339
00:18:49,630 --> 00:18:50,850
Ishizaki!

340
00:18:50,850 --> 00:18:54,730
The cockroaches keep comin' 
outta the woodwork.

341
00:18:54,730 --> 00:18:58,240
You'd better back off the smack 
talk on the second-years!

342
00:18:58,240 --> 00:19:01,160
If you want to get out of here alive, 
you should lay off, Ishizaki.

343
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:03,910
Wh-Why are you stopping me?

344
00:19:03,910 --> 00:19:06,670
I know you very well.

345
00:19:06,670 --> 00:19:10,920
Hosen... you're quite 
a celebrity back home.

346
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:14,340
Y-You've heard of him, Ryuen-san?

347
00:19:14,610 --> 00:19:18,630
Though I didn't expect him to look 
like such a slack-jawed fool.

348
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:21,440
Fancy meeting you here.

349
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:24,390
I've heard more than I 
ever cared to about you.

350
00:19:24,390 --> 00:19:29,930
But I didn't think the legendary Ryuen 
would be such a scrawny little weakling.

351
00:19:30,370 --> 00:19:33,940
And I can see you're all muscle, 
right up to the contents of your skull.

352
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:37,780
I tried a few times to head up 
your way and murder your ass,

353
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:39,930
but you got scared and hid out, I guess.

354
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:42,920
You were lucky.

355
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:44,230
If you'd actually found me,

356
00:19:44,230 --> 00:19:47,950
you wouldn't be able to run 
your mouth like this now.

357
00:19:47,950 --> 00:19:51,770
How about we settle all 
the trash talk right now?

358
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:54,960
Let's not.

359
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:58,710
I can't see what I'd gain from 
a fistfight with a gorilla.

360
00:19:58,710 --> 00:20:02,220
You're not going to defend us 
from the first-years at all?

361
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:05,720
We can finish this anytime, after all.

362
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:08,470
Hey, come back and play, Ryuen.

363
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:10,480
Nah, I don't think so.

364
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:11,230
In that case...

365
00:20:16,570 --> 00:20:18,020
Just try and get her free!

366
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:21,110
C'mon, spectators! 
You can try me all at once!

367
00:20:21,110 --> 00:20:22,450
Are you insane?

368
00:20:22,450 --> 00:20:23,950
Damn it!

369
00:20:23,950 --> 00:20:25,890
Hosen-kun, stop it now.

370
00:20:27,550 --> 00:20:31,100
The upperclassmen are conscious 
of the security cameras.

371
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:34,580
Going on a rampage here 
won't accomplish anything.

372
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:37,590
Yeah, I know. I'm just playin' around.

373
00:20:37,590 --> 00:20:41,850
If you insist on being reckless, 
I'll take actions of my own.

374
00:20:41,850 --> 00:20:45,250
Perhaps I'll make a certain 
something common knowledge.

375
00:20:50,990 --> 00:20:54,350
Threatening me takes guts, Nanase.

376
00:20:54,350 --> 00:20:58,360
But if you disappoint me, 
you'll pay for it.

377
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:00,860
When that happens, 
I'll be prepared for it.

378
00:21:01,270 --> 00:21:02,990
What's this all about, Hosen?

379
00:21:04,940 --> 00:21:07,620
Fighting shouldn't be done in the streets.

380
00:21:07,620 --> 00:21:10,550
This doesn't qualify as a fight.

381
00:21:10,550 --> 00:21:11,980
Let's go, Nanase.

382
00:21:12,330 --> 00:21:13,870
That seems wise.

383
00:21:19,180 --> 00:21:23,760
I'm ready to pair up when you're 
ready to grovel, Ryuen-paisen.

384
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:27,960
Unfortunately, I don't pair 
up with wild gorillas.

385
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,800
What a shame.

386
00:21:30,780 --> 00:21:32,660
See ya, Horikita.

387
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:37,060
I'm sorry for the trouble.

388
00:21:49,570 --> 00:21:53,030
<i>She was sizing me up.</i>

389
00:22:19,530 --> 00:22:25,330
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

390
00:23:29,390 --> 00:23:35,950
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term
